{
  "dom_id": "step-q104921",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Find all of the subsets of $A=\\{2,5,7\\}.$",
  "worked_solution": "To find every subset of $A,$ we list out every combination of elements within $A.$ \n\nWe can use the following diagram to visualize the process:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14243624/assets/13d6206f24dffc537422873c012ff5400ce6cde163e8e48a1c057736408299fd.png)\n\nNote that we must include the empty set since it is a subset of every set.\n\nBy doing this, we get\n\n$$\n∅,\\{2\\},\\{5\\},\\{7\\},\\{2,5\\},\\{2,7\\},\\{5,7\\},\\{2,5,7\\}.\n$$",
